      "seed_rule": "The render seed is derive_noise_seed(dataset_seed, 'render', font_key, str(case_index)). The corruption seed is derive_noise_seed(dataset_seed, 'variant', source_id, family, severity_level). Both are pure functions of documented inputs, so the same source and corruption configuration always reproduce the same realisation and two severity levels never share a random field.",
      "source_id": "src-<first 16 hex characters of the SHA-256 digest of the canonical source payload>. The payload distinguishes the text case identifier, the font identifier, the pinned font SHA-256, the generation configuration hash, the per-case render configuration hash, the render seed, the exact text and the text length. The identifier therefore changes if the case, the face, the font file, the renderer configuration or the generation configuration changes, and it never depends on directory traversal order, wall-clock time, absolute paths, runtime randomness or row ordering.",
